Why are Concurrent Collections Faster?

Instead of locking the whole collection,

they use smarter techniques like

Fine-grained locking
Lock striping (older ConcurrentHashMap implementations)
CAS (Compare-And-Swap)
Lock-free algorithms
Copy-on-write (for specific collections)

So multiple threads can work simultaneously depending on the collection.

Example
Vector
Thread 1 ---> LOCK

Thread 2 ---> Waiting

Thread 3 ---> Waiting

Only one thread.

ConcurrentHashMap
Thread 1 ---> Bucket 1

Thread 2 ---> Bucket 8

Thread 3 ---> Bucket 12

Multiple threads can work at the same time on different parts of the map.

Much faster.

