Interview Question
Why is CopyOnWriteArrayList useful?

Because

Reads are extremely fast.
Reads don't block each other.
Iterators never throw ConcurrentModificationException.
But what's the drawback?

Every write operation

add()

remove()

set()

copies the entire array.

If the array has

10,00,000 Elements

Adding one element copies all one million elements.

Very expensive.

When should we use CopyOnWriteArrayList?

Use it when

90% Reading

10% Writing

Examples

Configuration data
Cache of feature flags
List of listeners
Read-heavy applications
When NOT to use it?

Suppose

1000 Writes/sec

Terrible choice.

Because every write copies the array.

