ConcurrentHashMap

Most asked interview question.

Why not Hashtable?

Hashtable

Whole Table Lock

One thread.

ConcurrentHashMap

Allows much greater concurrency than Hashtable by avoiding a single global lock.

Modern implementations (Java 8+) use a combination of synchronized blocks on individual bins when needed and CAS operations for many updates.

Multiple threads can often update different parts of the map simultaneously.

Why ConcurrentHashMap doesn't allow null?

Suppose

map.get("Java");

Returns

null

Question

Did

Key doesn't exist?

OR

Key exists

↓

Value is null?

Impossible to distinguish safely in concurrent code.

So Java simply disallows null keys and null values.

Interview Question

Why does HashMap allow null but ConcurrentHashMap doesn't?

Answer

Because in concurrent environments a returned null could mean either "the key is absent" or "the value is null". Disallowing null removes this ambiguity.

